<svelte:head>
	<title>Uninstall · last30days-news</title>
	<meta
		name="description"
		content="Remove last30days-news installed with npm, npx, the installers, Docker or systemd, including its database and service files."
	/>
</svelte:head>

<script>
	import CopyCommand from '#lib/components/CopyCommand.svelte';
	import { UNINSTALL_PS1_URL, UNINSTALL_SH_URL } from '#lib/site';

	const dockerRemove = 'sudo docker rm -f last30days-news && sudo docker volume rm last30days-data';
	const dockerImage = 'sudo docker image rm ghcr.io/emmraan/last30days-news:latest';
	const systemdStop = 'sudo systemctl disable --now last30days-news';
	const systemdFiles = 'sudo rm /etc/systemd/system/last30days-news.service && sudo systemctl daemon-reload';
	const systemdData = 'sudo rm -rf /opt/last30days-news /var/lib/last30days-news && sudo rm -f /etc/last30days-news.env';
	const linuxData = 'rm -rf "${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/last30days-news"';
</script>

# Uninstall

This page covers local installs and VPS deployments. A Vercel deployment is removed in the Vercel dashboard; this page does not cover it.

Stop the app before removing anything. Removing the data directory deletes the database, saved API keys and settings. Keep a copy if you want the reading list later.

## Remove everything at once

One command removes every method it finds on the machine: the global npm package, cached npx copies, local data, the Docker container, volume and image, and a systemd unit. You do not need to know which method was used. Run it as your normal user, not with `sudo`; the script asks for sudo only for Docker and systemd files.

### Windows PowerShell

<CopyCommand command={`irm ${UNINSTALL_PS1_URL} | iex`} label="PowerShell" />

### macOS and Linux

<CopyCommand command={`curl -fsSL ${UNINSTALL_SH_URL} | sh`} label="Terminal" />

Caddy and Vercel settings are not touched. Remove a Caddy site block by hand, and remove a Vercel project in the Vercel dashboard.

## npm, npx and the installers

The Windows installer, the macOS/Linux installer and both npm commands create a global npm package. Remove it with npm:

<CopyCommand command="npm uninstall --global last30days-news" label="Terminal" />

`npx last30days-news` leaves a cached copy under npm's cache. Clear the npx cache when you also want that removed:

<CopyCommand command="npm cache clean --force" label="Terminal" />

This clears the whole npm cache, not only this package. npm downloads what it needs again on the next install.

## Local data

Delete the data directory for your platform. The app must be stopped first.

### Windows PowerShell

<CopyCommand command='Remove-Item -Recurse -Force "$env:APPDATA\last30days-news"' label="PowerShell" />

### macOS

<CopyCommand command='rm -rf "$HOME/Library/Application Support/last30days-news"' label="Terminal" />

### Linux

<CopyCommand command={linuxData} label="Terminal" />

If you set `L30_DATA_DIR`, delete that directory instead. This removes `db.sqlite` and its WAL files. Node.js and npm stay installed; remove them separately if you no longer need them.

## Docker

The automatic VPS installer and the manual Docker command use the same container and volume names. Stop and remove both:

<CopyCommand command={dockerRemove} label="Terminal" />

The volume contains the database. If you used a bind mount instead, delete that host directory yourself. The image can be removed after the container is gone:

<CopyCommand command={dockerImage} label="Terminal" />

## systemd

Stop and disable the service, then remove the unit and the files it uses:

<CopyCommand command={systemdStop} label="Terminal" />

<CopyCommand command={systemdFiles} label="Terminal" />

<CopyCommand command={systemdData} label="Terminal" />

The last command deletes `/var/lib/last30days-news`, which holds the database. Remove the Caddy site block too, then reload Caddy.

Remove the service user when no other service uses it:

<CopyCommand command="sudo userdel last30days" label="Terminal" />

## After uninstall

- Global npm installs have no background process or startup entry, so nothing else runs.
- Docker containers are removed, so they no longer restart.
- systemd no longer starts the service after a reboot.
- Vercel deployments are managed on Vercel.

To install again, start from [install](/docs/install).
